-- title:
--   Gotzmann persistence for ideals of maximal Hilbert growth
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $n$ and $m$ and a function $h : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N}$. For an ideal $I$ of $K[x_0,\dots,x_n] =$ `MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) K` and $d \in \mathbb{N}$, write $\mathrm{piece}\,I\,d$ for the quotient of the $K$-module of degree-$d$ homogeneous polynomials by those lying in $I$, i.e. $(K[x]/I)_d$. Assume two conditions on $h$, each for every $e \ge m$: (h₂) for every field $K$ (in `Type`) and every ideal $J$ of $K[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ which is the span of a set of $e$-th degree homogeneous polynomials, if $\dim_K \mathrm{piece}\,J\,e = h(e)$ then $\dim_K \mathrm{piece}\,J\,(e+1) \le h(e+1)$; and (h₃) there exist a field $K$ and such an ideal $J$ generated by forms of degree $e$ with $\dim_K \mathrm{piece}\,J\,e = h(e)$ and $\dim_K \mathrm{piece}\,J\,(e+1) = h(e+1)$. Let then $K$ be a field and $J$ an ideal of $K[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ generated by a set of homogeneous polynomials all of degree $m$, with $\dim_K \mathrm{piece}\,J\,m = h(m)$ and $\dim_K \mathrm{piece}\,J\,(m+1) = h(m+1)$. The conclusion is that $\dim_K \mathrm{piece}\,J\,e = h(e)$ for every $e \ge m$.
--
--   Hypotheses (h₂) and (h₃) say that $h(e+1)$ is exactly the maximal growth permitted by Macaulay's theorem for a quotient by an ideal generated in degree $e$ (the bound, and its attainment over an arbitrary field by a suitable monomial ideal), so the statement is Gotzmann's persistence theorem: an ideal generated in degree $m$ whose Hilbert function achieves the maximal growth from degree $m$ to degree $m+1$ continues to achieve it in all higher degrees. It is used to show that the maximal-growth condition propagates and, through that, in the construction of points of the Hilbert functor.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPolynomial_finrank_piece_eq_of_maximal_growth.lean

